WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.325
"Ah-choo!" Arthur sneezed loudly into his hands.

2
00:00:12.326 --> 00:00:16.075
"Arthur, don't you have a tissue?

3
00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:22.814
Please sneeze into your arm, not your hands," Mrs. MacPhee said.

4
00:00:22.815 --> 00:00:25.855
"Why?" Arthur asked.

5
00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:30.252
He held up his hands and wiggled his fingers.

6
00:00:30.253 --> 00:00:35.110
"I can catch the sneeze droplets better with my hands."

7
00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:43.770
"Cold germs spread very easily―especially after a sneeze," the teacher said.

8
00:00:43.771 --> 00:00:50.837
"Every time you touch something, you could spread your cold germs."

9
00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:56.856
"Eww!" Sarah said, leaning away from Arthur.

10
00:00:56.857 --> 00:01:04.315
"Rhinoviruses are the most common cold viruses," Mrs. MacPhee said.

11
00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:11.047
"They can live for up to 24 hours outside of the body.

12
00:01:11.048 --> 00:01:17.636
They can even live on things like computer keyboards and doorknobs."

13
00:01:17.637 --> 00:01:29.521
"So if I use the computer after Arthur, I might get a cold too?" Sarah asked.

14
00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:38.291
The teacher nodded. "Even hours after Arthur used it."

15
00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:43.833
"'Rhinovirus' sounds like 'rhinoceros!'" Cody said.

16
00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:47.367
The teacher laughed.

17
00:01:47.368 --> 00:01:57.191
"The word 'rhinovirus' comes from the Greek word for 'nose.'"

18
00:01:57.192 --> 00:02:03.895
"I've had four colds already this winter," Sarah complained.

19
00:02:03.896 --> 00:02:10.860
"Most children get eight to twelve colds a year," the teacher explained.

20
00:02:10.861 --> 00:02:17.868
"There are over two hundred different viruses that cause the common cold.

21
00:02:17.869 --> 00:02:22.533
Adults get only two to four colds each year.

22
00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:30.508
That's because they've already been exposed to many of the viruses."

23
00:02:30.509 --> 00:02:40.413
Cody put up his hand. "I read that sneeze droplets can travel almost two meters."

24
00:02:40.414 --> 00:02:46.210
Sarah frowned. "That's disgusting."

25
00:02:46.211 --> 00:02:54.431
"How do you think we can avoid catching a cold?" Mrs. MacPhee asked.

26
00:02:54.432 --> 00:03:01.217
"Stay two meters away from somebody who is about to sneeze?" Cody guessed.

27
00:03:01.218 --> 00:03:07.696
"That's not always possible," the teacher said.

28
00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:11.169
"Any other ideas?"

29
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:15.016
Sarah pointed to the sink at the back of the classroom.

30
00:03:15.017 --> 00:03:18.309
"Wash our hands with soap?"

31
00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:23.624
"Excellent idea, Sarah," Mrs. MacPhee said.

32
00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:30.481
"We should wash our hands in warm, soapy water for at least twenty seconds.

33
00:03:30.482 --> 00:03:33.304
This gets rid of the germs."

34
00:03:33.305 --> 00:03:43.004
Arthur put both hands over his nose and tilted his head back. "Ahh . . . ahh . . ."

35
00:03:43.005 --> 00:03:47.184
The other students all leaned away from Arthur.

36
00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:51.231
Arthur put down his hands and grinned.

37
00:03:51.232 --> 00:03:59.010
"Just kidding. I wanted to see if you were paying attention."

38
00:03:59.011 --> 00:04:05.151
"It's almost lunchtime. Everyone, please line up to wash your hands."

39
00:04:05.152 --> 00:04:08.911
Mrs. MacPhee smiled at Arthur.

40
00:04:08.912 --> 00:04:22.055
"Arthur, maybe you should go first!"

